Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.25.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.25.0 reproduces Stheno's out-of-frame gesture model 1:1 (reverse-engineered from Stheno.dylib: cardTrim / EdgeBarControlView / PanGestureSubType / finalCardCorner): the window is now the content area plus an 18 pt invisible trim ring on all four sides; edges drag the window, corners resize it proportionally with the opposite corner pinned (incremental accumulation kept - the anchor is only used for origin derivation), a double tap anywhere on the trim toggles the app picker, and the hosted app receives every touch inside the content area like before. The old inner strips and the corner grip are gone; the reload/close buttons float small and translucent at the content's top-right. Also fixes archive 27: FBSOpenApplicationService has no +sharedInstance (unrecognized selector) - it is now created via alloc/init, so tapping a not-running app really launches it and auto-hosts 2 s later. No new config keys; cfgVersion stays 20.
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
